{
  "slug": "letmewatch",
  "name": "Letmewatch",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Lets Claude analyze video files by extracting key frames using ffmpeg scene detection. Instead of processing video natively, the plugin captures only frames where visuals change significantly, timestamps each\none, and feeds them to Claude in batches. Works with screen recordings, bug reports, tutorials, and any video content. Includes optional audio transcription via whisper. Supports macOS, Linux, and Windows. Only\nrequires ffmpeg as an external dependency.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill** and **3 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `letmewatch` (Analyze video files by extracting key frames with scene detection)\n- **Commands** (3): `video-dir`, `video-last`, `video`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install letmewatch@claude-community` from `BinyaminEden/letmewatch`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
